re on e4 and d5, prepares castling, and doesn’t commit the pawn structure prematurely. Other moves like `d7-d6` are solid but slow, and `d7-d5` could lead to immediate tactical complications that may favor White given knights already developed. Since it’s early in the game, getting pieces out safely while keeping options open is wise.  \n\n**Answer:** N: g8-f6'}
