cing it to move and losing a tempo. It also secures some kingside space and can be followed by ...Rg8 or ...Kg7 to improve king safety. Other moves like c5-d4 open the position but might favor White's better-developed pieces. h5 is a solid, active move.  \n\nAnswer: P: h7-h5"}
